/-
Level-spherical eigenvectors of the right convolution, and the cut projector.

Two rows of the "the carrier is generated by level-invariant `archCut` vectors" story that
SET-AF104's `Cusp/{SpectrumDensity,ArchTypeProjector}.lean` set up:

* `exists_real_forall_rightConv_eq_smul_of_isLevelSphericalOfType` — a cuspidal form `φ` that
  is an eigenfunction of the right convolution by every level-spherical test function of
  archimedean type `tys` has a **real** eigenvalue, and the eigenvalue is *the same* for every
  such test function: `rightConv φ f = (real eigenvalue) • φ`.  This is the statement that the
  Hecke/convolution algebra acts on `φ` through a character once `φ` spans a one-dimensional
  `archCut`-type piece, and it is what makes the local parameters of a cusp form well defined.
* `exists_idempotent_cutProjector_of_isCompact` — for a compact open level subgroup `U`, the
  idempotent projector of SET-AF104B together with the arch-type projector of SET-AF104A gives a
  single idempotent `E` that cuts the carrier onto the `U`-invariant `archCut` piece
  (`E.comp E = E`, `E` fixes the piece, `E` maps into it, and `E` commutes with the cusp lifts).

The engine is the right-convolution action and its commutant
(`Adelic/RightConvComm/{Action,Level}.lean`, `RightConvCosetSum.lean`), the archimedean
approximation and spherical vectors (`ArchApproximation.lean`, `ArchSpherical.lean`), the
